    <h2>3. Information Stored Locally on Your Device</h2>
    <p>
        To perform business accounting, invoice generation, customer credit tracking, and stock management, the Application stores data locally on your device within an encrypted Android Room SQLite database:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Customer & Supplier Records:</strong> Names, contact numbers, and addresses that you manually enter for your shop records.</li>
        <li><strong>Ledger Transactions:</strong> Credit given (Udhaar / Debit), payments received (Jama / Credit), transaction dates, payment modes (Cash, UPI, Online, Bank Transfer), and notes.</li>
        <li><strong>Sales Invoices & Purchases:</strong> Bill numbers, items purchased, quantities, unit prices, discounts, and payment status.</li>
        <li><strong>Inventory & Stock:</strong> Item names, categories, cost prices, selling prices, and current stock counts.</li>
        <li><strong>Shop Profile:</strong> Shop name, owner name, business category, address, phone number, and optional UPI ID (used solely for printing on customer invoices).</li>
        <li><strong>Security App PIN:</strong> If you enable the 4-digit App Lock feature, your PIN is converted into a salted cryptographic <strong>SHA-256 hash</strong> on your device. The cleartext PIN is never stored or recorded.</li>
    </ul>

